      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Ectopic pregnancy is one of the ginecobstetric conditions that contribute to increased maternal mortality by 10 to 15% of cases. Ovarian ectopic pregnancy is one of the rare cases and represents up to 3% of ectopic pregnancies."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CASE",
          "content": "Female with 33 years old with lower abdominal pain, and pallor. Transvaginal ultrasound showed a live product with 15.3 weeks in left ovary and moderate hemoperitoneum. Exploratory laparotomy was performed with left salpingo-oophorectomy; postoperative course was satisfactory, discharged on the fourth day."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Ovarian pregnancy is a rare form of presentation. Preoperative diagnosis is difficult and must have a high level of diagnostic suspicion with physical examination and imaging studies. Treatment will vary according to clinical and diagnostic precocity."
        }
      ]},
